---
import TrainingLayout from "../../layouts/TrainingLayout.astro";
import Snippet from "../../components/training/Snippet.astro";
import LiveDemo from "../../components/training/LiveDemo.astro";
import ApiLink from "../../components/training/ApiLink.astro";
import ChapterLink from "../../components/training/ChapterLink.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/training/Callout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
---
<TrainingLayout slug="array-of-arrays">

  <h2 id="matrix">Every area as a two-dimensional array</h2>
  <p>
    Not every data source delivers objects. CSV files, spreadsheet exports, matrices from an API – they are rows of values.
    <ApiLink name="TableFactory.createTableModel" /> takes them directly:
  </p>
  <Code lang="text" title="public/data/orders.csv" code={`id,date,customer,country,city,product,category,quantity,price,total,status
1,2025-04-22,Dupont SA,Spain,Madrid,Docking Station,Accessories,18,230.15,4142.7,paid
2,2026-07-19,Kowalski Sp.,Spain,Madrid,Support Plan,Services,10,915.73,9157.3,paid
…`} />
  <Snippet file="demos/array-of-arrays.ts" region="csv" title="csv/csv-table.ts" />
  <Snippet file="demos/array-of-arrays.ts" region="model" />
  <LiveDemo name="array-of-arrays" title="orders.csv" height={380} caption="1,000 rows from a CSV file, with a totals row in the footer." />

  <h2 id="fields">The fields</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>headerData</code> and <code>footerData</code> are arrays of rows – <strong>several header rows</strong> are possible:
      <code>headerData: [["Order", "", "Amount", ""], ["ID", "Date", "Qty", "Total"]]</code>.</li>
    <li><code>bodyData</code> – the body rows; the factory wraps them into an <ApiLink name="AreaModelArrayOfArrays" />.</li>
    <li><code>columnSizes</code> – widths in pixels, when you don't need full <ChapterLink slug="column-definitions" label="ColumnDefs" />.</li>
  </ul>

  <Callout type="pitfall" title="footerData is static">
    <p>
      The footer row here is computed once. If the table is filtered or edited, it does not change. A footer that follows the
      visible rows is one option since 1.1.94 – <code>footerAggregates</code> (<ChapterLink slug="footer-totals" />).
    </p>
  </Callout>
  <Callout type="tip" title="Real CSV">
    <p>The split by comma above is enough for the demo data. For quoted fields (<code>"Smith, Ltd"</code>) use a CSV parser of
      your choice – the table only needs the resulting <code>string[][]</code>.</p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="next">Next</h2>
  <p>Grouped, multi-row headers that the user can collapse: <ChapterLink slug="header-groups" />.</p>
</TrainingLayout>
